# Who has to look at a change before it lands.
#
# Shaped after barakoCMS's: a catch-all, then explicit entries for the paths where a mistake is
# most expensive. The explicit ones are redundant while the catch-all names the same person, and
# they are kept anyway, so that narrowing the default later does not silently orphan them.
#
# The expensive paths here are not the API's. This is a browser client that ships as an image and
# holds a session, so the costly mistakes are in what runs with repository credentials, what the
# container does at start, and what decides whether the console will talk to a server at all.

*                           @arnelirobles

# CI, releases, and anything that runs with repository credentials. publish.yml alone touches a
# GHCR token, Docker Hub credentials and the playground SSH key in one run.
/.github/workflows/         @arnelirobles
/.github/codeql/            @arnelirobles
/scripts/                   @arnelirobles

# Session-time execution surface on a contributor's machine. Nothing here yet, listed because the
# moment there is, it should not arrive unreviewed.
/.claude/                   @arnelirobles

# The image and how it is configured at start. entrypoint.sh writes the file the browser reads its
# API URL from, so a mistake here points the console at the wrong backend without changing a line
# of application code.
/Dockerfile                 @arnelirobles
/entrypoint.sh              @arnelirobles
/next.config.ts             @arnelirobles

# Token handling and the refresh path. A wrong change here is a session bug for every user at once.
/src/lib/api.ts             @arnelirobles
/src/hooks/use-auth.ts      @arnelirobles

# Whether the console agrees to run at all. Widening the supported contract range without meaning
# to would let it drive an API it cannot, which is the failure this file exists to prevent.
/src/lib/api-contract.ts    @arnelirobles
